## fattn-tile-instance-dkq512-dv512.cu on gfx1030: no instance spills (66 to 230 VGPRs, occupancy 4 to 12)
# So D=128, D=256 and D=512 all spill on RDNA1 and none of them on RDNA2. One cause, every head size.

## What Vulkan has on this board, for the quantized-matmul comparison (vulkaninfo, RADV GFX1013, Mesa 26.1.8)
shaderIntegerDotProduct = true, but every integerDotProduct*Accelerated property = false
llama-bench Vulkan header on every 2026-09-15 run: "matrix cores: none", "int dot: 0"
# The Vulkan q4_K matvec shader (mul_mat_vec_q4_k.comp) unpacks nibbles with unpack8() and does float
# fma chains; it never touches integer dot. Its lead on quantized matmuls is formulation, not hardware.

## qualification of "RDNA1 only", from the gfx1030 side of the same sweep
gfx1030 D=256: one instance (4x2) spills 2 VGPRs, 12 bytes/lane; every other instance is clean
gfx1030 D=64:  the large-column instances spill 58 to 71 VGPRs, 236 to 288 bytes/lane
# So at D=128, 256 and 512 the spill is RDNA1-only. At D=64 RDNA2 spills modestly and RDNA1 badly
# (1048 VGPRs on the 64-column instance). No model measured here uses D=64.

