## candidate                 <64,1,false>  <64,1,true>  <8,8,false>            <16,4,false>           <8,8,true>
## (512,3,32,64) committed   137 / 544 B   125 / 336    0, vgpr 211, occ 4     0, vgpr 210, occ 4     83
## (512,3,32,128)            135 / 528     113 / 336    0, vgpr  96, occ 10    0, vgpr  95, occ 10    77
## (512,3,32,32)             165 / 544     123 / 320    52 / 156               51 / 152               82
## (512,2,32,64)             137 / 544     125 / 336    0, vgpr 211, occ 4     0, vgpr 210, occ 4     83   (identical: the occupancy hint changes nothing)
## (512,3,16,64), (512,3,16,128): do not compile, static assertion at fattn-tile.cuh:891
## No compiling row brings the ncols2 = 1 variant under about 115 spilled registers: each of its 64 columns
## carries its own K and V, where the GQA variants share them across ncols2 columns. The <32,1> instance is
## clean (237 VGPRs, no spill) under every candidate. nbatch_K 128 halves the register use of the GQA
## variants and lifts their occupancy from 4 to 10 waves per SIMD.

# ---- 2026-09-18 07:30: nbatch_K 256 on the D=128 rows ----
## rows 64 (and 32) -> nbatch_K 256: does not compile, static assertion at fattn-tile.cuh:745. 128 is the ceiling.
